+## Account mixed diagnostic
 
-Keep the existing simultaneous bursts as stress evidence. The next separate scenario uses 100 active accounts with the same 100-habit/two-year histories, arranged into 50 explicitly joined synthetic families. Four 30-second rounds schedule one personal mutation per account and one shared dated completion/Undo per family per round: 400 personal and 200 shared mutations. Alternate full/Undo so the final personal history and XP can be compared with the original fixture. Spread scheduled arrivals evenly within each round, record actual scheduling lateness, and do not silently slow arrivals to make the server pass.
+Run `node --import tsx scripts/infra/check-account-load.ts mixed-smoke`, then `node --import tsx scripts/infra/check-account-load.ts mixed`, separately from all other database/browser suites. The smaller mode has two accounts and one family; full mixed mode has 100 accounts with the same 100-habit/two-year histories, arranged into 50 explicitly joined synthetic families. It shares the burst diagnostic's fixed-test boundary, advisory lock, disk guard, private manifest, unchanged roles/pool/timeouts and exact cleanup.
 
-Use the current foreground group's 15-second metadata refresh cadence, including content reads after a revision change, for all 100 accounts. Measure the other member's observed shared state from server acknowledgment; retain unobserved states and observations beyond 15 seconds as failures. This is API/client-state convergence, not a browser paint or physical-device result. Keep private account history unavailable to the other member.
+Four 30-second rounds schedule one personal mutation per account and one shared dated completion/Undo per family per round: 400 personal and 200 shared mutations. Full/Undo alternate so final personal history and XP can be compared with the original fixture. Arrivals are spread within each round; both request latency and scheduling lateness are recorded. The gate includes lateness in accepted p95, and failed/deferred intentions remain separate rather than disappearing from the report.
 
-Capture immutable operation IDs/bodies before submission. A failed prior command must not be replaced or silently bypassed: report subsequent deferred intentions separately, recover the same sequence after measurement, then verify all receipts, final histories, XP and shared snapshots. Report first-attempt latency/failures, deferred arrivals, recovery and convergence separately. Preserve the existing roles, pool/timeouts and owner/group locks. Fixture cleanup must register exact synthetic group IDs and owners before creation, remove only those groups, then remove only this run's exact accounts; extend the protected crash-recovery manifest without storing invitation tokens or credentials.
+All accounts refresh group metadata every 15 seconds. The diagnostic uses the actual `SharedContent` reader and real API responses for content invalidation, errors and dated occurrence reads; a small metadata adapter retains the session's version fencing. Successful shared mutations immediately refresh their actor. The other member's observed state is timed from server acknowledgment. Missing observations and observations beyond 15 seconds fail convergence. This is API/client-state convergence, not browser paint or physical-device acceptance. The tool does not read another member's private account history.
